      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To examine the error rates for the sarcasm detection module and check latency issues across all instances on the legacy cluster, you would typically need to run scripts or commands that access Prometheus and Grafana - common tools used for metrics and monitoring. Assuming Prometheus is set up for instance metrics, we could use the PromQL (Prometheus Query Language) to fetch the required data:\n\n```shell\n# Example PromQL queries to be executed in Prometheus's REST API endpoint:\ncurl -g 'http://<Prometheus-Server-Address>/api/v1/query?query=nanotime_sector{instance=\"\"}'\n\ncurl -g 'http://<Prometheus-Server-Address>/api/v1/query?query=error_rates_by_instance{instance=\"*\"}'\ncurl -g 'http://<Prometheus-Server-Address>/api/v1/query?query=rate(panic{instance=\"*\"}[5m])'\n```\n\nAnd for Grafana, assuming an HTTP request on the Grafana dashboard API:\n\n```shell\ncurl -X GET --url 'http://<Grafana-Server-Address>/api/dashboards/uid/<Dashboard-UID>' -H 'Authorization: Bearer <Your-API",
